      "content": "Social democrats counter the self-ownership claim by arguing that individuals are never truly isolated; rather, their very capacity to exercise liberty depends on a prior collective agreement to maintain a just basic structure of institutions and resources. Drawing on thinkers like Rawls and Repetto, they posit that in a reasonable structure of society, no rational actor would reject a fair tax scheme if holding it as an acceptable alternative to a society where the living are left to fend for themselves against the convenience of the rich. This perspective reframes taxation not as an imposition on property, but as an investment in the shared foundations of social existence that actually protect the integrity of individual rights. By appealing to the moral fact that we all stand to receive benefits from the common institutions we participate in, social democracy argues that excluding others from the fruits of our labor violates the principle of fair equality of opportunity, making collective responsibility the very prerequisite for genuine individual freedom.",
